## Overview

Voice notes that transcribe while people talk: the transcript arrives speaker by speaker, and once recording stops an AI writes the summary and to-dos.

- Once in view it presses Record: after four speakers and 2 seconds of silence it stops by itself (about 15 seconds), writes the key points and 3 to-dos, and says "3 to-dos created" inside the stage.
- Stop works at any point while recording: only finished sentences reach the summary, and an unfinished one stays in the transcript; the key then becomes Record again.
- Choosing another recording while one is recording or summarizing settles it at once: what was heard is summarized in place, without a toast.
- The glow follows a simulated level and turns to its processing state while summarizing; the glow and the assistant avatar hold still when the stage is out of view, and the avatar moves only while summarizing, just after it finishes, or under the pointer.
- Every recording plays: the audio is synthesized in the page, with no microphone and no network request, and playback starts only from your click.
- Follow-ups answer inside the stage: Translate switches to a sample translation, while Send to Inbox and Set reminders only say they are samples; nothing is sent or scheduled.
- The transcript and the summary follow the newest content and stop while you scroll up; the page never moves.
- In the docs column (640–959px) the transcript sits above the summary, and from 960px the summary takes its own column with each side scrolling apart; narrow (< 640px) moves the recordings list behind a toggle in the header; reduced motion shows the finished recording with the glow off.

## Customization

- To use a real microphone, pass the stream from `useMicrophone` to TxVoiceBeam's `stream`; it analyses the level and bands itself and ignores `level`. Without a stream, give `level` a getter as this template does.
- Append the recognizer's partial results to TxStreamText's `content`, keep `streaming` true while the person speaks, and set it to false when the sentence ends.
- Keep the loudest level per time slice while recording and pass it as TxVoiceClip's `peaks`, so playback never decodes the audio; leave `durationMs` unset until the audio exists, because an unavailable clip holds its duration's width as a minimum and overflows a narrow column.
- For real recordings, turn the MediaRecorder Blob into an object URL for `src`, and release it with `URL.revokeObjectURL` when the recording changes and on unmount.
- To-do checks are stored by to-do id, not by language, so they survive switching to the translation.

